WEBVTT

00:00:08.125 --> 00:00:10.000
(Roaring)

00:00:10.125 --> 00:00:13.666
Oh! Hello. Beg your pardon.

00:00:16.166 --> 00:00:17.666
Aunt Lucy!

00:00:28.166 --> 00:00:29.583
(Gasps)

00:00:30.625 --> 00:00:32.083
Oh...

00:00:34.625 --> 00:00:36.458
(Roaring)

00:00:36.583 --> 00:00:38.166
(Echoing roar)

00:00:38.291 --> 00:00:40.291
- (Echoing roar)
- Oh!

00:00:40.875 --> 00:00:42.333
Aunt Lucy!

00:00:46.583 --> 00:00:48.083
(Roaring)

00:00:49.333 --> 00:00:51.291
(Echoing roar)

00:00:51.416 --> 00:00:52.791
Aunt Lucy!

00:00:54.916 --> 00:00:56.333
(Roaring)

00:01:01.541 --> 00:01:03.291
Almost there, Aunt Lucy!

00:01:03.416 --> 00:01:05.375
(Roaring)

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:06.833
(Echoing roar)

00:01:08.875 --> 00:01:10.333
Aunt Lucy!

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:16.875
I'm here!

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.041
(Echoing) I'm here! I'm here!

00:01:22.333 --> 00:01:24.041
I'm here!

00:01:25.125 --> 00:01:26.708
I'm here!

00:01:27.666 --> 00:01:29.083
I'm here!

00:01:30.333 --> 00:01:31.916
Aunt Lucy?

00:01:32.041 --> 00:01:33.791
(Echoing) Aunt Lucy?

00:01:33.916 --> 00:01:35.708
Aunt Lucy?

00:01:35.833 --> 00:01:37.041
Huh?

00:01:37.958 --> 00:01:40.541
You mean, all this time...

00:01:41.291 --> 00:01:43.625
...you were just an echo?

00:01:43.750 --> 00:01:46.833
(Echoing) Echo? Echo?

00:01:47.666 --> 00:01:48.875
Echo?

00:01:52.833 --> 00:01:54.250
(Sighs heavily)

00:02:00.833 --> 00:02:02.708
I'm sorry, Aunt Lucy.

00:02:03.541 --> 00:02:08.125
You found me all those years ago,
and now I can't find you.

00:02:10.541 --> 00:02:12.416
We're both lost.

00:02:15.125 --> 00:02:17.625
I don't want to say goodbye.

00:02:20.791 --> 00:02:21.875
(Hunter) So...

00:02:23.416 --> 00:02:26.750
...the bear showed the way.

00:02:26.875 --> 00:02:29.500
- Mr Hunter!
- But if this is El Dorado...

00:02:30.416 --> 00:02:33.958
...where is...
where is the gold?

00:02:34.083 --> 00:02:38.500
There is no gold, Mr Hunter.
And no Aunt Lucy.

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:43.625
There must be something,
some special mechanism,

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:48.291
that leads you to the... gold.

00:02:50.375 --> 00:02:51.666
A-ha!

00:02:52.750 --> 00:02:55.750
- What did I tell you?
- Oh?

00:03:03.291 --> 00:03:06.166
Strange Inca symbols.

00:03:06.958 --> 00:03:08.500
A triangle.

00:03:09.666 --> 00:03:12.791
A circle with an 'X' through it.

00:03:14.541 --> 00:03:16.791
"Dry clean only"?

00:03:17.916 --> 00:03:20.583
It's a washing label, Mr Hunter.

00:03:20.708 --> 00:03:23.540
"Barkridges of Kensington."

00:03:23.665 --> 00:03:26.833
Aunt Lucy's scarf!
She bought this in London.

00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:30.833
Are you... behind this wall?

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:33.958
Whoa! Oh!

00:03:35.665 --> 00:03:37.083
(Grunts)

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:46.290
This must open!

00:03:46.415 --> 00:03:48.083
(Groaning)

00:03:49.125 --> 00:03:50.500
Oh?

00:03:53.458 --> 00:03:56.750
(Gonzalo) The bear shows the way.

00:03:56.875 --> 00:03:58.540
Those clever Incas!

00:03:58.665 --> 00:04:02.458
The talisman... it must go in there.

00:04:02.583 --> 00:04:04.500
Take it from him.

00:04:04.625 --> 00:04:06.040
But...

00:04:07.125 --> 00:04:08.708
...it feels wrong.

00:04:08.833 --> 00:04:13.415
Wrong? Five hundred years
of searching for gold is wrong?

00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:18.708
But... I have made a promise to Gina...

00:04:18.833 --> 00:04:21.250
Forget about Gina.

00:04:22.625 --> 00:04:24.875
Take the talisman.

00:04:26.083 --> 00:04:28.375
Kill the bear!

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:30.583
Give me the talisman!

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:34.208
Talisman, Mr Hunter?

00:04:34.333 --> 00:04:35.665
Hand it over.

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:37.833
No.

00:04:37.958 --> 00:04:41.333
I said... hand it over.

00:04:41.458 --> 00:04:44.790
Promise we can go in together.

00:04:44.915 --> 00:04:48.333
Well, the thing about that, Bear,

00:04:48.458 --> 00:04:52.790
is that Cabotos don't share!

00:04:57.165 --> 00:04:59.375
(Chuckles)

00:04:59.500 --> 00:05:01.125
An umbrella?

00:05:01.250 --> 00:05:05.375
Not just any brolly.
The Windsorman Deluxe.

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:09.625
London's finest, Mr Hunter!

00:05:13.625 --> 00:05:15.000
(Gasps)

00:05:15.125 --> 00:05:17.250
Uh... Uh...

00:05:20.708 --> 00:05:25.875
Apparently, they bought this plane
for the Pope's visit in 1985.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:30.583
- It's got its MOT and everything?
- It's got a papal blessing.

00:05:30.708 --> 00:05:32.583
(Rattling and beeping)

00:05:32.708 --> 00:05:34.208
(Engine dies)

00:05:34.791 --> 00:05:36.291
(Beeping)

00:05:36.416 --> 00:05:37.833
(Engine starts)

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:42.250
- Look!
- What?

00:05:45.416 --> 00:05:46.750
It's Paddington!

00:05:50.708 --> 00:05:51.500
Bear!

00:05:53.833 --> 00:05:55.916
Oh! Spiky Red One!

00:05:59.708 --> 00:06:02.083
- Reverend Mother, can you land?
- It'll be tight.

00:06:02.208 --> 00:06:03.708
Yes!

00:06:04.666 --> 00:06:07.166
- Where are you, Bear?
- Oops!

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:13.083
- (Alarm beeping)
- The landing gear's jammed.

00:06:13.208 --> 00:06:16.458
One of you will have to lift
that panel in the floor,

00:06:16.583 --> 00:06:19.458
and turn the manual release.

00:06:20.208 --> 00:06:21.916
It's all right, I'll do it.

00:06:24.625 --> 00:06:26.125
(Mrs Brown) Go on, darling!

00:06:28.291 --> 00:06:30.125
Ooh!

00:06:32.750 --> 00:06:35.708
Any-anyone happen to have
a very large tumbler?

00:06:35.833 --> 00:06:37.708
Come on, Henry!

00:06:39.083 --> 00:06:40.750
(Sniffing)

00:06:40.875 --> 00:06:42.875
I can smell the marmalade.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:44.833
(Sniffing)

00:06:47.208 --> 00:06:48.958
Oh! Hello.

00:06:55.708 --> 00:06:57.958
Sorry, Mr Hunter!

